  "goodToKnow": "Der Akzent has three common meanings: a regional or foreign accent (mit österreichischem Akzent), an emphasis or highlight (einen Akzent setzen), and an accent mark such as é or è. Akzente setzen means to set priorities or add highlights, in design too: ein roter Akzent im Raum. Note the stress on the last syllable: ak-ZENT. For a regional way of speaking, Germans also use der Dialekt."
